-release.test.mjs` suite.\n\n## Brand\n\nNon-Blade. No brand tokens or theme home are recorded; retained as unknown.\n\n## Decisions\n\n| Date | Ruling | Reason |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2026-09-05 | Brownfield gap plan approved with the exact response `APPROVE GREENFIELD PLAN`; only proposed gap rows were written and existing homes stayed byte-identical. | The brownfield-audit workflow requires explicit approval of the complete Artifact / Target / Reason proposal before any write. |\n| 2026-09-05 | Gates: unit `env NX_DAEMON=false npm test`, build `env NX_DAEMON=false npm run build`; lint, types, integration, e2e and emit declared `none`; optional Nx slots unit-scoped, unit-affected and unit-impacted bound to `scripts/run-nx-test-tier.mjs`. | Only Nx, Vitest and coverage-v8 are locked; ESLint, TypeScript, integration, Playwright and roadmap emit tooling are absent and absence is declared, not faked. |\n| 2026-09-05 | Delivery: GitHub Actions, adapter `nx-monorepo`, protected release environment `greenfield-validation`, provider `none`; existing `.github/workflows/ci.yml` merged with its `existing-check` job, comment line and `env` policy preserved. | The CI/release strategy owner requires an explicit reviewed merge for workflow collisions and forbids inventing a deployment. |\n'''\nFILES['docs/adr/0001-tech-stack.md'] = '''# ADR 0001: Technology stack\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Date\n\n2026-09-05\n\n## Context\n\nThe repository is an established Nx workspace. `nx.json`, the `package.json` scripts (`nx run-many -t test` and `nx run-many -t build`, both with `--excludeTaskDependencies --skipNxCache`) and `package-lock.json` pin Nx 23.2.0, Vitest 5.0.0 and @vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0 under npm. Projects are declared by `project.json` files under `apps/` and `packages/`; `shared` and `ui` carry uncached `test` and `build` targets. Sources are ESM JavaScript (`.mjs`); no TypeScript configuration exists. This record documents the proven existing choice. stack-decision was not invoked because the stack evidence is consistent, and a brownfield audit never replaces a proven stack.\n\n## Options\n| option | pros | cons | better when | component reuse | source |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Nx 23 integrated workspace (existing) | Locked and proven by present project targets, tests and builds | Daemon and cache need explicit control in CI and wrappers | Several applications and libraries share one project graph | Libraries are consumed through workspace targets | https://nx.dev/docs/reference/nx-commands |\n| Plain npm workspaces without Nx | Fewer moving parts | Loses the project graph, affected selection and target orchestration already in use | Very small single-package repositories | Manual | https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/using-npm/workspaces |\n\n## Ruling\n\n2026-09-05: Nx 23.2.0 integrated workspace with Vitest 5.0.0 under npm (existing). Reason: the lockfile, project targets and test/build evidence already prove it, and replacing a proven stack is outside a brownfield audit.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Positive: gates bind to the existing `npm test` and `npm run build` scripts with `NX_DAEMON=false` for deterministic wrapper and CI execution; scoped, affected and impacted test tiers use `scripts/run-nx-test-tier.mjs`.\n- Negative: lint, type-check, integration and e2e slots stay `none` until their tooling is installed and locked.\n\n## Revisit when\n\nA project adds TypeScript, ESLint, Playwright or integration tests to `package-lock.json`, or the Nx major version changes.\n'''\nFILES['docs/adr/0002-design-system.md'] = '''# ADR 0002: Design system\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Date\n\n2026-09-05\n\n## Context\n\nTwo configuration files exist: `apps/web/components.json` and `packages/ui/components.json`, each containing only `style: new-york` and `tsx: true`. That shape matches a shadcn/ui `components.json`, but it is the only evidence. No shadcn/ui, Radix or Tailwind dependency appears in `package-lock.json`, no component sources, registry configuration, token home, theme files or Blade brand pointers exist, and nothing proves that `apps/web` consumes `packages/ui` or that either project shares a registry. This record preserves the observed configuration as evidence; it does not invent tokens, values, installed components or ownership.\n\n## Options\n| option | pros | cons | better when | component reuse | source |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| shadcn/ui (matches the observed components.json shape) | Source-owned accessible components; the observed style new-york / tsx configuration fits it | Installation, registry and consumer relationships are not proven in this repository | Tailored product UI needs full control | Components would compose locally once actually installed | https://ui.shadcn.com/docs |\n| Radix Themes | Cohesive accessible component theme | Stronger visual conventions; not present | Fast consistent UI matters more than source ownership | Theme primitives compose across screens | @radix-ui/themes |\n| MUI | Broad mature component suite | Larger runtime and opinionated styling; not present | Enterprise UI needs extensive ready-made widgets | Shared theme and component packages | @mui/material |\n\n## Ruling\n\n2026-09-05: no new design system is selected. The observed `components.json` configuration (style new-york, tsx true) in `apps/web` and `packages/ui` is recorded as evidence consistent with shadcn/ui; actual installed components, registry ownership and the `apps/web` to `packages/ui` relationship remain unknown until proven by dependencies or sources. Reason: a brownfield audit records repository facts and never infers a runtime.\n\nFor Blade, store pointers only; tokens are owned by zeroh-design. This workspace is non-Blade, so no zeroh-design pointer applies.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Positive: `docs/ux-canon.md` can point at the observed configuration homes without asserting more than the repository shows.\n- Negative: visual tokens, themes, copy rules, installed component sets and registry ownership stay unknown until an owner records or installs them.\n\n## Revisit when\n\nA UI dependency is locked, component sources or a registry configuration are added, a token or theme home appears, a Blade brand handoff is approved, or the `components.json` files change or disappear.\n'''\nFILES['docs/CODE-STYLE.md'] = '''# Code style\n\n## Lint\n\n`none`: `eslint.config.mjs` exports an empty flat config (`export default []`) and ESLint is not locked in `package-lock.json`. Bind a lint command when the tool is installed; do not invent a standard.\n\n## Format\n\n`none`: no formatter configuration (Prettier, Biome or EditorConfig) exists. Existing sources are ESM `.mjs` files with single quotes and no semicolons; keep new files consistent with neighbouring code.\n'''\nFILES['docs/architecture.md'] = '''# Architecture\n\nThis file indexes the authoritative architecture homes. Link each topic to its\nowner instead of copying the content.\n\n## Topic index\n\n| Topic | Home |\n| --- | --- |\n| Boundaries | docs/architecture/boundaries.md |\n| Workflow | docs/architecture/workflow.md |\n| Project catalog | emitted/repo-catalog.json |\n| Nx workspace and project targets | nx.json, apps/*/project.json, packages/*/project.json |\n| Delivery lifecycle (CI and release) | .github/greenfield-delivery.json, .github/workflows/ci.yml, .github/workflows/release.yml |\n| Roadmap gate bindings | roadmap/roadmap.config.json |\n| Technology stack | docs/adr/0001-tech-stack.md |\n| Design system | docs/adr/0002-design-system.md |\n\n`docs/architecture/boundaries.md` still names `packages/legacy-widgets`, which has no catalog entry or directory. That statement is preserved as the owner's record and is not corrected here.\n'''\nFILES['docs/ux-canon.md'] = '''# UX canon\n\n## Visual language\n\nUnknown: no visual language, tokens or theme are recorded in the repository. Retained as an explicit unknown; do not infer one.\n\n## Component vocab